  "notes": "Two independent positioner failures occurred in sequence on the same valve: 2ZC1111A (feedback signal quality issue, not attributed to the official cause code) and 2ZC1111B (foreign material/debris, the actual root cause per Block 13 cause code B). Both are modeled as separate FailureMode nodes with a shared downstream consequence (valve failing shut), consistent with rule 5's parallel-trigger guidance. Only 2ZC1111B's foreign-material failure is linked CAUSED_BY the official Cause node, since that is what the narrative identifies as the root cause driving code B. AFW is modeled as an involved/operated system (manually initiated as part of recovery), not a BACKED_UP_BY relationship to a specific failure chain, since it did not prevent the trip but restored SG level afterward. No previous similar occurrences found per Section G, so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge is created."
